From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Darren Huang" <darren.huang@advantech.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tc956x: qcom: Accept RGMII and RGMII-ID from phy-mode

tc956x_platform_port_interface_overlay() only maps phy-mode "sgmii"
and rejects everything else, so a port wired to an RGMII PHY can only
be configured through the macX_interface module parameter array, which
is indexed by probe order and shared by every port not listed in
tc956x_eth_ports_bdf.

AOM-2721 eMAC1 drives a Realtek RTL8211F over RGMII with PHY-side
delays. Left at the eMAC1 default (SGMII) the PHY links up but no
frame is received. Map "rgmii" and "rgmii-id" as well, with the same
MDC clock and clause-22 access as the port 1 defaults.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor specific]
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/toshiba/tc956x/tc956x_qcom.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/toshiba/tc956x/tc956x_qcom.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/toshiba/tc956x/tc956x_qcom.c
index c1ef1cb..7d5d954 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/toshiba/tc956x/tc956x_qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/toshiba/tc956x/tc956x_qcom.c
@@ -110,6 +110,16 @@ int tc956x_platform_port_interface_overlay(struct device *dev,
 		res->c45_state = false;
 		res->mdc_clk = TC956XMAC_XGMAC_MDC_CSR_62;
 		break;
+	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII:
+		res->port_interface = ENABLE_RGMII_INTERFACE;
+		res->c45_state = false;
+		res->mdc_clk = TC956XMAC_XGMAC_MDC_CSR_62;
+		break;
+	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_ID:
+		res->port_interface = ENABLE_RGMII_ID_INTERFACE;
+		res->c45_state = false;
+		res->mdc_clk = TC956XMAC_XGMAC_MDC_CSR_62;
+		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
